Prop10. $0$ is even.
Prop20. Let $n$ be an even natural number. Then $n + 1$ is odd.
Prop30. Let $n$ be an odd natural number. Then $n + 1$ is even.
Prop40. Every natural number is even or odd.
Prop50. For all natural numbers $n$, $n$ is not even and odd.
Prop60. For all natural numbers $n$, $n + 0 = n$.
Prop70. $1$ is odd.
Prop80. $2$ is even.
Prop90. Let $n \in \Natural$. Then if $n$ is even and prime, then $n = 2$.
Prop100. Let $a , b , c \in \Integer$ such that $a + b + c = 0$. Then $a \times b \times c < 0$.
Prop110. Let $a , c \in \Integer$ such that $a$ and $c$ are odd. Then for all integers $b$, $a \times b + b \times c$ is even.
Prop120. Let $a , b \in \Integer$. Then $a \times b$ is even, if and only if $a$ or $b$ is even.
Prop130. Let $x , y \in \Integer$. Then if $x \times y$ is odd, then $x$ and $y$ are odd.
Definition. Let $x , y \in \Integer$. Then $x$ and $y$ have the same parity, if both $x$ is even and $y$ is even or both $x$ is odd and $y$ is odd.
Prop140. Let $x$ and $y$ be integers. Then $x$ and $y$ have the same parity, if and only if $x + y$ is even.
Prop150. Let $n \in \Natural$. Then $n ^ {3}- n$ is even.
Prop160. Let $a , b \in \Integer$. Then if $a + b$ and $a \times b$ have the same parity, then $a$ and $b$ are even.
Prop170. For all natural numbers $x$, $x$ is not even and odd.
